{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "fXcedbB280", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764810, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "l7UjlEbxwF", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Iraq / Death Toll / Attacks", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) The Pentagon\u2019s announcement that 1,000 Americans have died fighting in Iraq reported. \n (Pentagon: Jim Miklaszewski) The increasing violence in Iraq reviewed; scenes shown of fighting between US troops and Iraqi insurgents in Baghdad\u2019s Sadr City, a roadside bombing and a US air strike in Fallujah; details given of the pullout of US troops from 5 Iraqi cities under pressure from the Iraqi government and the US plan to retake cities if negotiations fail. [Secretary of Defense Donald RUMSFELD&nbsp- predicts an increase in violence as elections approach.] [US Army retired Gen. Barry McCAFFREY&#134;- says we\u2019ve ceded huge parts of the country to insurgent control.] [Brookings Institution Michael O\u2019HANLON&#134;&#134;- notes the Iraqis are not well-trained.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764811, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "buCqUN0X2a", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Decision 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Iraq War", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced. \n (Columbia, Missouri: David Gregory) The issue of the Iraq war in the presidential election featured; details given of President Bush\u2019s focus on Senator John Kerry\u2019s inconsistencies about Iraq. [KERRY \u2013 reacts to the death toll in Iraq reaching 1,000; comments on the cost of the war.] [BUSH \u2013 criticizes Kerry.] [May, 2003, former presidential candidate Howard DEAN \u2013 says this was the wrong war at the wrong time.] [May, 2003, KERRY \u2013 says it was the right decision to disarm Iraqi President Saddam Hussein.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63190.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764812, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "N0ZUoYxc3F", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Economy / Federal Deficit", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) The CBO\u2019s projection for the federal budget deficit cited. \n (Capitol: Chip Reid) The differing political views on the record federal deficit examined; statement from President Bush\u2019s campaign quoted [Senator Kent CONRAD&#134;- complains about the deficit.] [CBO director Douglas HOLTZ-EAKIN&#134;- notes the economic burden of the retiring baby-boom generation.]", "segment_duration": 120, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764813, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "4Ltbq92iT8", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Russia / School Standoff / Video / Survivors", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (Moscow: Jim Maceda) Dramatic videotape recorded by the Islamic militants who took over a school in Beslan, Russia, featured; scenes shown of hostages inside the school gym, terrorists wiring explosives, a demonstration in Moscow, where protestors called for Russian President Vladimir Putin to crack down on terrorism, & funeral processions in Beslan.   (Studio: Brian Williams) The accounts of 14-year-old Aslan Dzarasov&#134; and his 12-year-old brother Soslan Dzarasov&#134;, who survived the massacre at the school, presented in their own word. [DZARASOVs {thru translator}&nbsp- describe what happened from the time the militants took over until their escape when the building began to explode.]", "segment_duration": 250, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63450.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764814, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "IhWpfNkbrM", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Brian Williams)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63700.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764815, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "iVGO9mqW42", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "(Commercial: US Postal Service; Marie Callender\u2019s; Cialis; Quaker Oatmeal; Capital One; \"Today\"; \"Hardball.\")", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63730.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764816, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "uG4qCr0d0X", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "In Depth (12 Ways to Make America Safer) Part II", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Special week-long series on steps to make a terrorist attack less likely continued. \n (Staten Island, New York: Fred Francis) Calls for increasing inspections of containers that arrive in the nation\u2019s ports featured; details given of the proposal to put agents in overseas ports. [US Customs deputy chief inspector Kevin McCABE&#134;- notes most of the people in the port saw the World Trade Center towers fall.] [Port expert Stephen FLYNN&#134;&#134;- explains safety precautions in Hong Kong.] [Secretary of Homeland Security Tom RIDGE \u2013 praises the work at the National Targeting Center, which aims to pinpoint high-risk cargo.]", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63880.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764817, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764810, "segment_id": "yFhN7hLoo6", "segment_broadcast_id": "ENwt3LW9Up", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Brian Williams)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "64030.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764818, "net